==English==

===Etymology===
From {{term|head}} + {{term|way}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|headways|-}}

# {{countable}} The [[clearance]] beneath an object, such as an [[arch]], [[ceiling]] or [[bridge]]; [[headroom]].
# {{nautical}} [[forward|Forward]] [[motion]], or its [[rate]].
# {{countable|transport}} The [[interval]] of [[time]] or [[distance]] between the fronts of two [[vehicles]] (e.g. [[bus]]es) moving in succession in the same [[direction]], especially along the same pre-determined [[route]].
# {{uncountable|figuratively}} [[progress|Progress]] toward a [[goal]].

====Derived terms====
* [[make headway]]

